course: dictionary
lesson: 15822
title: Uncouple: pulling joined things apart
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To couple means to join two things together, like two railway carriages. To uncouple means to undo that join and separate them. The prefix un- often means "undo", so uncouple means "undo the coupling".
explain: Look at the words around it to work out the meaning. «The workers uncoupled the last carriage at the station.» Workers would not uncouple something that stays joined, so the carriage must be pulled away from the rest of the train.
explain: The same word works with ideas. «The teacher uncoupled the two questions so each could be answered alone.» Here the questions were linked, and the teacher treated them separately. Always check: if you swap in "separated", does the sentence still make sense? If it does, you have the meaning.
fact: Uncouple is a verb. Its other forms are uncouples, uncoupled and uncoupling.
fact: «Uncouple» means to separate two things that were joined together.
fact: «The farmer uncoupled the trailer from the tractor» means he unhooked the trailer so the two were no longer joined.
fact: In formal language, to uncouple two ideas means to treat them separately, as if they were not linked.
fact: The prefix un- often means "undo", so you can think of uncouple as "undo the coupling".
exercise: «The workers uncoupled the last carriage at the station.» What does uncoupled mean? | *Separated the carriage from the rest of the train | Joined a new carriage on | Cleaned the train's windows | Painted the carriage
exercise: Dad says, «The tractor must uncouple the trailer before we go to the shed.» What does uncouple mean here? | Drive faster than the trailer | Make the trailer bigger | *Unhook and separate the trailer from the tractor | Paint the trailer
exercise: «The carriages were coupled together before the trip.» Find and copy the word that means joined. | carriages | *coupled | together | before
test: «The teacher uncoupled the two ideas so the class could think about each one alone.» What does uncouple mean in this sentence? | Wrote them down twice | Forgot them | Mixed them up | *Separated them and treated them apart
test: Why would a worker uncouple carriages at a station? | To hide the train | To paint the carriages | *To separate some carriages from the train | To make the train go faster
exam: Which word means the same as uncouple, when two joined things are pulled apart? | *Separate | Connect | Attach | Join
